.\" oxdump.1 - manual page for the oxdump IL2CPP dumper.
.\" Render/preview with:  man -l docs/oxdump.1
.\" Lint with:            groff -man -Tutf8 -ww docs/oxdump.1 >/dev/null
.TH OXDUMP 1 "2026-07-26" "oxdump 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oxdump \- extract IL2CPP metadata from Unity games into a dump archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oxdump
.I metadata binary
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-\-skip\-pair\-check ]
.RB [ \-\-xref\-names ]
.br
.B oxdump
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B oxdump
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oxdump
is a fast, dependency-free C++17 reimplementation of a Unity IL2CPP dumper.
Given a game's
.I global-metadata.dat
and its compiled IL2CPP image
.RI ( libil2cpp.so ,
.IR UnityFramework ,
or
.IR GameAssembly.dll ),
it reconstructs the type system \(em classes, fields, methods, and their runtime
addresses \(em and writes a set of human- and tool-readable files into a single
ZIP archive.
.PP
The two input files may be given in either order; each is identified by its
signature
.RB ( AF\ 1B\ B1\ FA
for metadata, and ELF / Mach-O / PE magic for the binary), so argument
position does not matter.
.PP
Three binary formats are supported and share one pipeline:
ELF64 (Android / Linux), Mach-O 64-bit (iOS / macOS, including FAT archives),
and PE64 (Windows). The encryption key applied to the metadata header is
recovered automatically from header invariants; several transforms
(XOR, ADD32, SUB32, XOR+ROL, XOR+index) are tried in turn. When the header
itself is unreadable, a
.I headerless
mode rebuilds the section map by scanning the file body.
.PP
.B oxdump
never emits a silently corrupt dump: known-bad situations (mismatched file
pair, packed library, unsupported chained fixups) are detected and explained
rather than ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write the dump archive to
.I file
instead of the default
.IR oxide_dump.zip .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose log: show how the key, metadata tables, and MetadataRegistration were
located, plus per-stage details.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode: print only the path to the produced archive on standard output.
Useful in scripts. Suppresses the progress log on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-pair\-check
Do not abort when the metadata and binary appear to come from different
builds. The resulting types may be wrong; use only when you know the pairing
is correct.
.TP
.B \-\-xref\-names
Collect naming hints for obfuscated methods by disassembling method prologues
and following references to string literals. Adds a few seconds to the run.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; the dump archive was written.
.TP
.B 1
Failure while parsing the metadata or the binary (unreadable header that
headerless mode could not recover, missing MetadataRegistration, packed
library), or an internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: missing or unrecognized arguments, or an unknown flag.
.TP
.B 3
The metadata and binary are from different builds and
.B \-\-skip\-pair\-check
was not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Dump an Android game to the default archive:
.PP
.RS
.EX
oxdump global-metadata.dat libil2cpp.so
.EE
.RE
.PP
Choose the output name and show a verbose log:
.PP
.RS
.EX
oxdump global-metadata.dat libil2cpp.so -o dump.zip -v
.EE
.RE
.PP
Windows game (arguments in any order), quiet output for a script:
.PP
.RS
.EX
archive=$(oxdump GameAssembly.dll global-metadata.dat -q)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Force a dump despite a mismatched pair, with string-based name hints:
.PP
.RS
.EX
oxdump meta.dat UnityFramework --skip-pair-check --xref-names
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
The output archive contains:
.TP
.B dump.cs
Readable class tree with fields and methods.
.TP
.B il2cpp.h
C structures with offsets (Il2CppDumper-compatible).
.TP
.B script.json
Method addresses for IDA / Ghidra / Binary Ninja.
.TP
.B offsets.h
Namespace-per-class header with
.B constexpr
field offsets for C++ tooling.
.TP
.B offsets.cs
Parallel C# static classes for C# tooling.
.TP
.B types.txt
Flat, grep-friendly index of all classes.
.TP
.B REPORT.txt
What was detected and how, including headerless notes.
.SH BUGS
Chained fixups (iOS 15+ / arm64e Mach-O) are not supported; such builds are
rejected with a clear message rather than mis-parsed. End-to-end PE support has
been validated only against a synthetic image, not a real
.IR GameAssembly.dll .
In headerless mode, method parameters and the assembly (Image[]) list are not
recovered. Report issues with the output of a
.B \-\-verbose
run attached.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR objdump (1),
.BR readelf (1)
.PP
Project documentation: see
.I README.md
in the source distribution.
